  "content": "### Strategy (aim: 5 real friendships, not just acquaintances)\nWe’ll reduce uncertainty first by identifying *specific* Austin/online venues with recurring attendance (best for repeat exposure), then set up a repeatable system to convert repeated hangouts into deeper 1:1 connections.\n\n### What ‘success’ means operationally\n- **Lead** = someone you’ve met twice and have contact info (text/IG/Discord).\n- **Friendship-in-progress** = you’ve done **1:1** (coffee, hike, game night) at least once.\n- **New friend** = you’ve done **2+** meaningful hangouts and can comfortably invite each other to something.\n\n### Execution structure\n- Pick **2 primary pipelines** (e.g., board games + hiking) plus **1 light pipeline** (indie shows) to avoid spreading too thin.\n- Commit to **2 recurring events/week** for 6–8 weeks (repetition is the moat).\n- Use a simple follow-up script + a weekly “friendship funnel” review so momentum doesn’t die like Bumble BFF chats.\n\n### Deliverable from this plan\nA concrete 6–8 week schedule with: venues/events to attend, outreach scripts, and a tracking + accountability loop aimed at reliably producing 5 friends.",
